              "count": 1,
              "items": [
                {
                  "id": "",
                  "status": "",
                  "title": "compliance: T4 is assessed clause by clause against the SPEC_V2 section 12 gate on the post-#831 record. Clause 1 ('an injected failure yields exactly one coach card and one remedy'): the remedy's missing effect (v1-p6-1, P0) is fixed — `coach.remedy` applies the bounded effect in its own transaction (block/move/retry/repull; ask is the gate and writes no effect) and `process_runs.start` refuses a blocked card or a pending ask (409 `coach_blocked` / `coach_ask_pending`), proved by `crates/actions/tests/coach.rs::{a_block_remedy_stops_the_next_dispatch, a_retry_remedy_lets_the_next_dispatch_run, a_move_remedy_places_the_card}` with the v1 ledger receipt at 26b47b61cfe735b5b891afb4dd0d5ea6e63434e0. Clause 1 remains refuted as a universal by v1-p6-4 (P1, open). Clause 2 ('a repeat signature escalates') stands as proved by `::a_repeat_signature_escalates_instead_of_a_second_card`. Clause 3 ('no coach card about a coach card') stands as proved by `::a_failed_coach_run_never_opens_a_coach_card` and `::a_nested_coach_run_is_refused`. Clause 4 ('a systemic class opens a kata') stands as proved only as a `kata.open` process start by `::a_systemic_class_opens_one_kata` with `::a_transient_class_opens_no_kata`, and v1-p6-2 remains open. Open findings after this unit: v1-p6-2, v1-p6-3, v1-p6-4, v1-p6-5 (P1) and v1-p6-6 (P2), all tracked in docs/evidence/v1-conformance-findings.json; no P0 remains for T4. The rework's acceptance instrument is `acceptance/programme/T4.toml`."
                }
              ],
